      "description": "Fine dispersed droplets (a few µm to tens of µm) are captured by the fibres of the coalescing media, merge with other captured droplets and leave the outer surface as large drops. Large drops settle quickly (Stokes: velocity ∝ d²) into the water boot. Surfactants can disarm coalescing media, so they are selected for the interfacial tension of the system.",
